# ── what each kind of ground is made of: mineral share, mineral share, ... (parts per 100) ──

@mix temperate
name: Land of a temperate world
grain-mm: 0.1..0.5
clasts: pebble 4..64 0.08, cobble 64..256 0.03, boulder 256..1500 0.005
minerals: quartz 25, albite 18, orthoclase 14, kaolinite 12, augite 6, biotite 5, calcite 8, hematite 5, magnetite 3, forsterite 2, gypsum 2

@mix desert
name: Dry rocky ground
grain-mm: 0.2..0.5
clasts: granule 2..4 0.3, pebble 4..64 0.45, cobble 64..256 0.1, boulder 256..2000 0.02
minerals: quartz 22, hematite 14, albite 14, augite 14, forsterite 10, enstatite 6, magnetite 6, gypsum 6, halite 4, calcite 4

@mix lava
name: Fresh basalt and lava rock
grain-mm: 0.2..1
clasts: pebble 4..64 0.3, cobble 64..256 0.25, boulder 256..3000 0.1
minerals: augite 28, anorthite 26, forsterite 18, fayalite 6, magnetite 10, ilmenite 6, sulfur 4, pyrite 2

@mix snowball
name: Frozen ground
grain-mm: 0.2..1
clasts: pebble 4..64 0.1, cobble 64..256 0.05, boulder 256..2000 0.02
minerals: water-ice 70, dry-ice 10, nitrogen-ice 5, methane-ice 5, forsterite 5, enstatite 5

@mix moon
name: Moon ground
grain-mm: 0.04..0.1
clasts: pebble 4..64 0.05, cobble 64..256 0.02, boulder 256..4000 0.01
minerals: anorthite 40, augite 22, forsterite 14, ilmenite 14, fayalite 5, quartz 5

@mix tidally-locked
name: Ground of a tidally locked world
grain-mm: 0.1..0.5
clasts: pebble 4..64 0.25, cobble 64..256 0.06, boulder 256..2000 0.015
minerals: augite 22, anorthite 18, quartz 14, hematite 14, forsterite 12, water-ice 10, magnetite 10

@mix ocean
name: Sea floor
grain-mm: 0.01..0.06
clasts: pebble 4..64 0.02
minerals: augite 30, anorthite 25, forsterite 15, calcite 15, kaolinite 10, pyrite 5

@mix melt
name: Molten rock (a lava lake or flow, about 1,100 to 1,200 C)
grain-mm: 0..0
minerals: basalt-melt 100

@mix core
name: A giant planet's core (rock, iron and ice under enormous pressure)
grain-mm: 0.1..0.5
minerals: forsterite 30, magnetite 25, enstatite 15, water-ice 20, methane-ice 5, pyrite 5

@mix sea
name: The sea
grain-mm: 0..0
minerals: sea-water 100

@mix ice
name: Sea ice and ice sheets
grain-mm: 0.2..1
minerals: water-ice 100

# ── what lies on a grain's surface, everywhere, at its real size (soil science: clay platelets 0.2 to 2 um across,
#   iron-oxide coatings 0.1 to 1 um, iron-oxide nanoparticles 5 to 50 nm, and a film of water one or two molecules thick
#   from the air on every mineral surface; and specks of silt, 4 to 62 um, stuck on sand grains by clay and water).
#   mineral: ground means one of that ground's own minerals. life: yes only on a living world; aspect: how many times
#   longer than wide (a rod). size-km: smallest to largest across; chance: how many of its cells hold one
#   (a cell is 'spacing' of its largest size, 4 if not given: clay coats much of a sand grain, so it is packed close); mineral: what it is made of (you go into its own atoms); shape: flat (a plate or a
#   skin, its thickness a share of its width: kaolinite plates about 1/15, coatings thinner), round, or molecule (drawn atom by atom from its mineral, with its bond length in nm and bond angle in degrees).
@surface silt
name: A speck of silt stuck to the grain
mineral: ground
size-km: 4e-9 6.2e-8
chance: 0.5
spacing: 2.5
shape: round
about: a tiny grain of the same ground, 4 to 62 micrometres across | held on by clay and the water film | wind and water carry it as dust and mud

@surface bacterium-rod
name: A rod-shaped bacterium (a bacillus)
mineral: cell-matter
size-km: 1e-9 5e-9
chance: 0.25
spacing: 3
shape: round
aspect: 3.5
life: yes
about: a single living cell, 1 to 5 micrometres long | soil holds about a billion bacteria in every gram | it feeds on what the water brings past the grain

@surface bacterium-coccus
name: A round bacterium (a coccus)
mineral: cell-matter
size-km: 5e-10 2e-9
chance: 0.25
spacing: 3
shape: round
life: yes
about: a single living cell, 0.5 to 2 micrometres across | often in pairs, chains or clusters

@surface biofilm
name: A biofilm (a mat of microbes in their slime)
mineral: cell-matter
size-km: 5e-9 3e-8
chance: 0.2
spacing: 3
shape: flat
thickness: 0.05
life: yes
about: microbes living together in a skin of their own slime | it holds water and food to the grain | most soil microbes live in films like this

@surface clay-platelet
name: A clay platelet (kaolinite)
mineral: kaolinite
size-km: 2e-10 2e-9
chance: 0.85
spacing: 1.6
shape: flat
thickness: 0.07
about: a thin six-sided plate, Al2Si2O5(OH)4 | left by water slowly weathering feldspar

@surface iron-coating
name: An iron-oxide coating
mineral: hematite
size-km: 1e-10 1e-9
chance: 0.6
spacing: 2
shape: flat
thickness: 0.03
about: a skin of iron oxide (hematite, goethite) | it colours sand red, orange and yellow

@surface nanoparticle
name: An iron-oxide nanoparticle
mineral: hematite
size-km: 5e-12 5e-11
chance: 0.6
spacing: 2.5
shape: round
about: a speck of hematite or goethite, Fe2O3 / FeOOH | a few thousand atoms of iron and oxygen

@surface water
name: A water molecule of the surface film
mineral: water-ice
size-km: 2.8e-13 3.2e-13
chance: 0.6
shape: molecule
bond-nm: 0.0957
angle: 104.5
about: H2O, bent at 104.5 degrees | from the air: every mineral surface wears a film | one or two molecules thick
